---
const sections = [
  { label: "Everyday story", href: "/projects/snnjotter/everyday-story" },
  { label: "Engineering puzzle", href: "/projects/snnjotter/engineering-puzzle" },
  { label: "Pipeline", href: "/projects/snnjotter/pipeline" },
  { label: "Glossary", href: "/projects/snnjotter/glossary" },
  { label: "Roadmap", href: "/projects/snnjotter/roadmap" },
];
---

<article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-10 sm:py-14">
  <header class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-primary/25 bg-surface px-6 py-9 text-center sm:px-10 sm:py-12">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-bold leading-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">SNNJotter</h1>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-white/80 sm:text-lg">
      A friendly notebook for my capstone: <span class="font-semibold text-white">FPGA-Accelerated Spiking Neural Networks for Real-Time Biomedical Signal Inference.</span>
    </p>
  </header>

  <section class="mt-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.035] p-5 sm:p-6" aria-labelledby="preface-title">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-primary">Preface</p>
    <h2 id="preface-title" class="mt-2 font-serif text-xl font-bold text-white">Why I opened the notebook</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/75">When friends or connections ask what I’m working on, I don’t want to hand them a long explanation full of jargon. So I made SNNJotter: a peek into my notebook while I figure things out, one idea at a time.</p>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/75">As an undergrad exploring Spiking Neural Networks, the word “spikes” has become a constant buzzword in my world. And because this project works with human heartbeat data, I want the big picture to make sense to everyday people too—not just people who already speak chip-design.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mt-8" aria-labelledby="contents-title">
    <h2 id="contents-title" class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-white sm:text-3xl">Table of contents</h2>
    <nav class="mt-4" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <ul class="divide-y divide-white/10 border-y border-white/10">
        {sections.map((section) => (
          <li>
            <a
              href={section.href}
              class="block py-3 text-base font-medium text-primary underline decoration-primary/40 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-white focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
            >
              {section.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-8 border-t border-white/10 pt-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-white/60">
    These are learning notes about a capstone workflow—not medical advice, a clinical tool, or a report of experimental results.
  </p>
</article>
